From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pi-hrx-fabric <fabric@1bit.local>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:53:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] accel/amdxdna: a closing context must not condemn the
 recovered array

aie2_tdr_recover_all() power-cycles the NPU after a TDR and then walks every
hwctx to restart it. One of them can be the context of a client that is
already closing: its heap no longer has a host buffer address (the client's
VMAs are gone), so aie2_hwctx_restart() refuses it with -ENODEV before it ever
talks to the firmware. The walk counted that as a recovery failure, which sets
hw_dead, and every later create_context/submit on the box is then refused
-ENODEV until the module is reloaded - although the power-cycle itself
succeeded and the array was healthy again.

Measured on strixhalo 2026-11-04 21:50:23 (kernel 7.4.0-rc1-1bit, module
56AB94758C18FEEC838D18C), real TDR under an NPU serve:

  aie2_tdr_recover_all: Array stopped dispatching, power-cycling NPU to recover
  aie2_hw_reset: NPU firmware unhealthy: power-cycling NPU
  aie2_hwctx_restart: hwctx.544293.15 has no host buffer address, cannot restart it
  aie2_tdr_resume_hwctx: hwctx.544293.15 restart failed, ret -19
  aie2_tdr_recover_all: NPU array is unusable until the driver is reloaded:
      TDR recovery failed (0, a context could not be restarted)

followed by ten aie2_create_context refusals from other processes in the next
21 s. The same firmware capture (Context ID 15, DPU PC 0xffffffff, Context PC
0x28b060ad, sub command ID 0) is what the c21/c22/c24 appliance runs produce, so
this escalation is the difference between "one request died" and "the NPU is
gone for every lane until a reload".

A context that is being torn down is not a recovery failure: skip its restart
(aie2_hwctx_restart() has already unpaused its jobs, so a waiter fails rather
than hangs) and keep the recovered array usable.

Signed-off-by: bong-water-water-bong <bong-water-water-bong@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_tdr.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_tdr.c b/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_tdr.c
index 4cc3d461..7fb950e6 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_tdr.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/amdxdna/aie2_tdr.c
@@ -122,11 +122,32 @@ struct aie2_tdr_resume_arg {
 static int aie2_tdr_resume_hwctx(struct amdxdna_hwctx *hwctx, void *arg)
 {
 	struct aie2_tdr_resume_arg *rarg = arg;
+	struct amdxdna_dev *xdna = rarg->xdna;
 	int ret;
 
-	ret = aie2_hwctx_restart(rarg->xdna, hwctx);
+	ret = aie2_hwctx_restart(xdna, hwctx);
 	if (ret) {
-		XDNA_ERR(rarg->xdna, "%s restart failed, ret %d", hwctx->name, ret);
+		/*
+		 * A context whose client is already tearing down has no host buffer
+		 * address left to map (the client's VMAs are gone), so it cannot be
+		 * restarted - and does not need to be: the process it belongs to is
+		 * gone, and aie2_hwctx_restart() unpaused its jobs before returning,
+		 * so anything still waiting on it fails instead of hanging.
+		 *
+		 * Counting this as a recovery failure is what turned one dying
+		 * context into "the NPU array is unusable until the driver is
+		 * reloaded" for every other client on the box: measured 2026-11-04
+		 * 21:50:23 on strixhalo, a TDR recovery whose power-cycle SUCCEEDED
+		 * (ret 0) was reported as failed because of this one context, and ten
+		 * later opens from other processes were refused -ENODEV.
+		 */
+		if (amdxdna_obj_dma_addr(hwctx->priv->heap) == AMDXDNA_INVALID_ADDR) {
+			XDNA_WARN(xdna,
+				  "%s has no host buffer address (client closing): not restarting it, the recovered array stays usable",
+				  hwctx->name);
+			return 0;
+		}
+		XDNA_ERR(xdna, "%s restart failed, ret %d", hwctx->name, ret);
 		rarg->failed = true;
 	}
 
-- 
2.53.0

